column4:
Yes, it outlines the measures together with our action plan, where have a quite strong focus on private sector. Here are some measures we are planning to implement in the two upcoming years:
Mapping the need for open data in the private sector and making such data available;
Carrying out a wider communication campaign to inform about open data and the ways it can be reused;
Providing monetary support  for the development of services based on open data.

column7:
We have extended our national metadata standard which is based on DCAT-AP to include a separate attribute used to denote dataset as high-value dataset. Updated metadata standard is accessible here: https://www.kratid.ee/_files/ugd/980182_87343e9f929143b1a566d1c96791ec09.pdf. Using metadata standard is mandatory for all public sector organisations and basis for the open data portal. Example: high-value-dataset-category.rdf
